#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""La notice (story 107, cycle 57; a hook, an absurd logic pushed step by step, an escalation through the whole country, a reversal, a dry last line).
This man only wants to check the dose of his medicine. He unfolds the leaflet and, like everybody, cannot fold it back: it covers the kitchen, then
the block, the street, the town and the country. Whoever reads it catches its side effects: the street itches, the town falls asleep at noon, the
country empties the bakeries, even the health minister walks like a crab. The weather forecast: « overcast, with small print ». The doctors overflow,
the whole country is ill and not one pill was swallowed: they only read it. At the far end, on a cliff over the sea, the last line says to ask the
pharmacist. His pharmacist folds the whole country in two seconds (a world record) and everybody is cured at once, no prescription. He finally asks
the dose: « One a day. » It was drawn on the box, big. He unfolds the leaflet again. To check. It slaps him in the face, like the first time.
Running gag (the dose was always in view, never mentioned): the brick-size white pill box (noPillBox) is in every shot of him (S01, S01b, S02, S02b,
S14, S14b, S15, S15b by its edge, S16, S16b), always held or stood square to the camera, its only marking one big white pill and one big yellow sun:
one a day. He never opens it to take a pill (S10: nobody in the country took one either). By ear « vérifier la dose » (S01) comes back in « demandé
la dose » (S14) and « Pour vérifier » (S16b); « Impossible de la replier » (S02) is answered by « a tout replié » (S12); « En gros » (S15) answers
« des petits caractères » (S06b). The last shot replays S02's slap: the same paper « flap », the leaflet flat over his face like a mask, the box held
up beside it, and the whole story is about to restart.
Staging (natural look; a cut every 0.7 to 2.2 s, long lines split into b/c shots on their words):
S01 the kitchen, morning, at his table: he holds the box up to his chest square to us; his neck stretches like rubber toward it to check (a squint,
a tremble), snaps back on « dose » with a squash. S01b a lower three-quarter: the lid flips, he pulls the tiny folded leaflet out, one shake, FLAP: it
bursts open flat over the table with an overshoot and a ripple and settles on it; he is blown back (stretch, hair up), the box still up in his left
hand. S02 high over the table: he folds it in half (both hands carry the edge over in an arc, his arms stretched), it puffs up like a pillow, he slams
it flat with both mittens (a squash), it springs open twice as big and flies into his face: the leaflet flat over his face like a mask (noFaceSheet),
his head knocked back, arms flailing (never still). S02b the kitchen papered from floor to ceiling, the paper draped over the fridge, the counter and
the cupboards, curling at the top: his head pops out of a heap of paper with a cork's squash (the petals spring out), then the box pops out beside it,
square to us; blinks, his eyes slide to the wall. S03 a building front from the far pavement: tongues of lined paper burst out of its windows one
after the other from the top floor, the whole building swells twice. S03b the street at pavement height: the leaflet rolls down the pavement toward
us like a carpet, a pigeon running on top of the roll, flapping to keep its balance. S04 four passers-by bent over the paper on the pavement read it
like typewriters: their heads sweep along a line together and snap back (two bells). S04b low over the paper: the word DÉMANGEAISONS pops up off it
like a pop-up book card (an overshoot), held a second above the captions; their heads recoil above it, then lean in to read. S04c all four spring up
and scratch at once: her back against a lamp post, a baguette down his back, both hands in her hair, a foot rubbing his calf. S05 a street corner under
the paper sky: a waiter with his tray, a cyclist by his bike and an old lady snap their heads up to read the sky, their eyes sweeping together; a street
clock with no figures. S05b on « Somnolence » huge yawns go down the row, then they fall asleep standing (heads drooping, the tray tilting), sleep
letters rise; on « midi » the clock's minute hand races round and stops with the hour hand straight up (a chime): nobody wakes. S06 a rooftop terrace
with a TV camera on a tripod: the weather presenter's umbrella springs open with an overshoot, she presents to the camera. S06b she points up with a
rubber arm that stretches into the sky and pumps; the camera tilts up to the paper ceiling, tiny grey lines, its curled edge flapping over the roofs.
S07 a bakery front: five customers bent over the paper on the pavement; on « Fringale » their bellies balloon with a growl, their heads snap to the door
and they dash in one after the other. S07b they burst out of the door one after the other hugging armfuls of baguettes, cheeks stuffed. S07c the baker
alone behind his counter, bare shelves of empty baskets: the last crumb tips off the top shelf and bounces down; his eyes follow it, he sags. S08 the
steps of a plain building (no flag, no emblem): the doors burst open, the minister and two aides step out, read the paper on the landing and on
« marcher » turn into crabs: knees bent, mittens up clacking like pincers, one sideways hop down. S08b closer, tracking with them: the minister crabs
sideways down the steps, perfectly serious, the aides behind in step, a pigeon crabbing along the bottom step. S09 a doctor's surgery built from the
office set (no cross anywhere): the tally board is full to its frame; he winds up and his rubber arm shoots across to squeeze one more stroke on the
very edge of the frame; the board shudders; he dusts his hands. S09b the waiting room on lined paper: one patient scratching, one asleep upright with
sleep letters, one crabbing across. S10 close on the doctor: an oversized blister pack pops up to the lens, every pill still sealed; one eyebrow up.
S10b the three patients freeze mid-symptom (three frames), then slowly look down at the paper under their feet, then up at us. S11 a sea cliff: the
corner of the giant sheet flaps over the edge; a hiker on hands and knees peers at it through a big magnifying glass; a gust lifts his hat. S11b from
over the sea, looking down at the corner: the last line fills the frame in two lines, DEMANDEZ CONSEIL / À VOTRE PHARMACIEN, the magnifying glass sweeping
along it, the hiker's face above. S12 a plain pharmacy front with a white and green capsule sign (no cross, no digit, no lettering): the pharmacist in
his white coat and round glasses crouches, grabs the edge of the paper at his door and flicks it like a tablecloth (a whole-body stretch). S12b looking
up the street: the paper sky snaps away over the rooftops like a roller blind, blue sky behind (REPLIÉE). S12c close in front of the pharmacy: the whole
sheet folded into a tiny square in his palm (it lands with a bounce); he pushes his glasses up; behind him a referee in a tracksuit pumps a card with
only a laurel wreath on it and blows his whistle on « Record ». S13 the street under a blue sky, five people: two scratchers, a sleeping waiter, the
minister and an aide crabbing; on « guéri » all of them pop straight at once with a single ding and look round. S13b the minister and the aide look
at their mittens (no longer pincers), at each other, and shrug together, heads sinking. S14 the pharmacy counter, a V two-shot: he hops up holding the
box out toward the pharmacist, square to us, all hope; the pharmacist leans in and squints at it. S14b the pharmacist's arm stretches across and taps
the drawing once with one finger (the box jolts, his head bobs) and he says « Un par jour » (lip flaps). S15 extreme close on the box: the big white pill
and the big yellow sun, a slow push in; his thumbs tap it once. S15b his face, blank: his eyes go down to the box and back, one slow blink. S16 the
counter again, high and in front as in S02: he flips the lid, pulls the tiny leaflet out, shakes it: FLAP, it springs open in front of him and slaps flat
over his face like a mask, the box held up beside it, square to us. S16b a little closer, held: the paper over his face breathes in and out; behind the
counter the pharmacist slowly takes off his round glasses and pinches the bridge of his nose, shakes his head, then looks at us.
Props (engine/props_notice.js, cycle 57): noLeaflet, noFaceSheet, noPillBox, noPaperRoom, noFacade, noPaperCarpet, noWordCard, noPaperSky, noTerrace,
noUmbrella, noArmful, noBakeryCounter, noSteps, noBlister, noCliff, noDrape, noPharmacy, noPharmaCounter, noLaurelCard, noChalkStroke, noZzz; reused:
ttTileOffset (props_tartine), bakeryFront (props_flaque), newsCam and streetClock (props_centime), magnifier (props_champagne), pigeon (props_porte),
serviceTray (props_cafe), table, chair, desk, bicycle, streetLamp, baguette, tallyBoard, glasses, whistle (props.js); sets kitchenDay, parisStreet,
office, whiteVoid, seaSurface. Never pharmacyCross nor the hospital set (a cross); the doctor's surgery is the office set.
Lessons applied from the start: Looney deformation on every accent (the rubber neck and arms, the squash and stretch of every pop, burst, slam and slap,
anticipation crouches, the typewriter heads, the cork pop, the overshooting pop-up word and umbrella, the crab hops); every action starts in the first
0.3 s of its shot; blinks and breathing on holds (life()); no raised arm held still (the pointing arm pumps, the pincers clack, the card pumps);
carried and moving objects are one world prop each, hands guided onto them (box, leaflet, baguettes, umbrella, blister, magnifier, card, tray, square);
the face sheet is attached to his head; look targets at head height or 'camera', pupils for the rest; word timings from timeline.json through st.at
(words from 0, printed beside their times); every cut set just under its frame (the frame index, then floored to 4 decimals); cameras checked with
project() (CHECKS: heads out of the caption band 0.77-0.83 and the card band 0.07-0.18); flat floor paper with a polygon offset; kitchenDay with
ttTileOffset; distinct models for every secondary character, five at most per shot; new props prefixed no; sound names checked against
audio3.py/audio.py/mix.py; no organisation, brand, flag, emblem, cross, insignia, digit or currency on screen; French only (BOULANGERIE, DÉMANGEAISONS,
DEMANDEZ CONSEIL / À VOTRE PHARMACIEN); the satire aims at the leaflet, never at a group; nobody hurt."""
from story_kit import *
import math

st = Story('notice', look='natural')
st.plan([('S01', 'L01', 0), ('S01b', 'L01', 6), ('S02', 'L02', 0), ('S02b', 'L02', 4), ('S03', 'L03', 0), ('S03b', 'L03', 2), ('S04', 'L04', 0), ('S04b', 'L04', 4),
         ('S04c', 'L04', 8), ('S05', 'L05', 0), ('S05b', 'L05', 5), ('S06', 'L06', 0), ('S06b', 'L06', 4), ('S07', 'L07', 0), ('S07b', 'L07', 6), ('S07c', 'L07', 10),
         ('S08', 'L08', 0), ('S08b', 'L08', 5), ('S09', 'L09', 0), ('S09b', 'L09', 3), ('S10', 'L10', 0), ('S10b', 'L10', 3), ('S11', 'L11', 0), ('S11b', 'L11', 2),
         ('S12', 'L12', 0), ('S12b', 'L12', 5), ('S12c', 'L12', 8), ('S13', 'L13', 0), ('S13b', 'L13', 6), ('S14', 'L14', 0), ('S14b', 'L14', 7), ('S15', 'L15', 0),
         ('S15b', 'L15', 4), ('S16', 'L16', 0), ('S16b', 'L16', 5)])
# every cut just under its frame: st.cut rounds to 4 decimals (53/30 -> 1.7667, after the frame: its first image would show the shot before); take the
# frame index and floor its time instead (1.7666: frame 53 belongs to the new shot)
FL = lambda v: math.floor(round(v * 30) / 30 * 10000) / 10000
st.SH = {sid: (FL(a), FL(b) if b < st.total else b) for sid, (a, b) in st.SH.items()}

PI = math.pi
def r(v, n=3): return round(v, n)
def add(a, b): return [r(a[i] + b[i]) for i in range(3)]
def lerp3(a, b, u): return [r(a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * u) for i in range(3)]
def yaw(src, dst): return r(math.degrees(math.atan2(dst[0] - src[0], dst[2] - src[2])), 1)
def fwd(ry): return [math.sin(math.radians(ry)), 0.0, math.cos(math.radians(ry))]
def right(ry): return [-math.cos(math.radians(ry)), 0.0, math.sin(math.radians(ry))]
def off(p, ry, f=0.0, s=0.0, y=0.0): F, R = fwd(ry), right(ry); return [r(p[0] + F[0] * f + R[0] * s), r(p[1] + y), r(p[2] + F[2] * f + R[2] * s)]
CHECKS = []
def chk(sid, frm, look, lens, pts):
    CHECKS.append(f"{sid}: " + ' | '.join(f"{n} {project(frm, look, lens, p)}" for n, p in pts.items()))
def chkc(sid, c, pts, end=False):
    frm, look = (c.get('to') or c['from'], c.get('lookAt2') or c['lookAt']) if end else (c['from'], c['lookAt'])
    chk(sid + ('>' if end else ''), frm, look, c['lens'], pts)
def W(sid, lid, i):
    # word timings from timeline.json: st.at counts the words from 0; the word is printed beside its time
    t = st.at(sid, lid, i); CHECKS.append(f"{sid} « {st.L[lid]['words'][i]['w']} » at {t}"); return t
EZ = {'linear': lambda u: u, 'inOut': lambda u: 2 * u * u if u < 0.5 else 1 - (-2 * u + 2) ** 2 / 2, 'out': lambda u: 1 - (1 - u) ** 3, 'in': lambda u: u ** 3}
def track(p0, moves):
    # where a prop moved by `to` keys is at t (each move starts where the last one ended; eases as the engine's): hands follow it exactly
    def at_(t):
        p = list(p0)
        for t0, to, d, e in sorted(moves, key=lambda m: m[0]):
            if t < t0: break
            u = EZ[e](1.0 if d <= 0 else min(1.0, (t - t0) / d)); p = [p[i] + (to[i] - p[i]) * u for i in range(3)]
        return [r(v) for v in p]
    return at_
def MOVES(moves): return [k(t0, to=list(to), dur=d, ease=e) for t0, to, d, e in moves]
def FALL(t0, p0, p1, dur, n=4):
    # a drop by gravity: linear `to` keys at the u^2 positions
    return [(r(t0 + dur * (i - 1) / n), lerp3(p0, p1, (i / n) ** 2), r(dur / n), 'linear') for i in range(1, n + 1)]
def R5(p, w=1, s=0.0): return [*p, w, s]
def FIT(frm, pts, back=False, **kw):
    # the aim and the lens that hold every point (heads with a margin of 0.12 of the width, above the captions): fit() / fitBack() of the kit
    kw.setdefault('margin', 0.12); kw.setdefault('top', 0.12); kw.setdefault('bottom', 0.78); kw.setdefault('lenses', range(30, 57))
    if back: f, look, lens = fitBack(frm, pts, **kw)
    else: f = frm; look, lens, _ = fit(frm, pts, **kw)
    assert lens, f'no lens fits from {frm}'
    return [r(v) for v in f], [r(v) for v in look], lens
def HAND(R=None, L=None, hr='grip', hl='rest', tipR=0.0, tipL=0.0, **x):
    return {'reach': {**({'R': R5(R, 1, tipR)} if R else {}), **({'L': R5(L, 1, tipL)} if L else {})}, 'hands': {'R': hr, 'L': hl}, 'hip': 0, **x}
def blink(t, face, keep=None): return [k(t, toon={**(keep or {}), 'face': {**face, 'lid': 1.0}}, toonDur=0.05), k(r(t + 0.1), toon={**(keep or {}), 'face': face}, toonDur=0.06)]
def life(t0, t1, face, keep=None, ph=0.0, blinks=(), period=0.9, amp=0.013):
    # a moving hold: slow breathing keys that carry the face and the hands (a toon key is a whole state), clear of the blinks
    out, bl, t_, i = [], sorted(blinks), t0 + ph, 0
    while t_ < t1 - 0.1:
        if not any(-0.04 < t_ - b < 0.2 for b in bl):
            q = [r(1 - amp * 0.4, 4), r(1 + amp, 4), r(1 - amp * 0.4, 4)] if i % 2 == 0 else [r(1 + amp * 0.3, 4), r(1 - amp * 0.6, 4), r(1 + amp * 0.3, 4)]
            out.append(k(r(t_), toon={**(keep or {}), 'sq': q, 'face': face}, toonDur=r(period * 0.8), toonEase='inOut'))
        t_ += period / 2; i += 1
    for b in bl: out += blink(r(b), face, keep)
    return out
def TALK(t0, t1, face, keep=None, step=0.1, nod=0.05, tilt=0.0):
    # lip flaps for somebody who speaks (never the hero): open / o / line shapes, small nods
    out, t_, i = [], t0, 0
    while t_ < t1 - 0.04:
        m = ['open', 'o', 'line', 'open', 'smirk'][i % 5]
        bd = {**(keep or {}).get('bend', {}), 'neck': [r(nod if i % 3 == 0 else -nod * 0.5), tilt, 0, 1, None]}
        out.append(k(r(t_), toon={**(keep or {}), 'bend': bd, 'face': {**face, 'mouth': m, 'jaw': 0.25 if m in ('open', 'o') else 0.0}}, toonDur=r(step * 0.7)))
        t_ += step; i += 1
    return out

# ============================== the box and the paper
BW, BH = 0.36, 0.24
def BOX(pid, pos, face_to, **o): return P(pid, 'noPillBox', pos=list(pos), ry=yaw(pos, face_to), opts=o)
def box_edges(p, ryb, side=0.2, back=0.025):
    # both mittens on the box's two short sides (its own width axis), a little behind its painted front
    ax, nz = [math.cos(math.radians(ryb)), 0.0, -math.sin(math.radians(ryb))], [math.sin(math.radians(ryb)), 0.0, math.cos(math.radians(ryb))]
    e = lambda sd: [r(p[0] + sd * side * ax[0] - back * nz[0]), r(p[1] - 0.02), r(p[2] + sd * side * ax[2] - back * nz[2])]
    return e(-1), e(1)
def BOXK(p, ryb, **x): R_, L_ = box_edges(p, ryb); return HAND(R_, L_, 'grip', 'grip', **x)
def BOXL(p, ryb, R=None, hr='open', **x): _, L_ = box_edges(p, ryb); return HAND(R, L_, hr, 'grip', **x)
def LEAF(pid, pos, **o): return P(pid, 'noLeaflet', pos=list(pos), rot=[-PI / 2, 0, 0], opts={'offset': True, 'shadow': False, **o})
def FLOORPAPER(pid, pos, w, h, ry=0, **o): return P(pid, 'noLeaflet', pos=list(pos), ry=ry, rot=[-PI / 2, r(math.radians(ry)), 0], rotOrder='YXZ', opts={'w': w, 'h': h, 'offset': True, 'shadow': False, 'creases': [6, 4], 'cols': 3, 'lh': 0.018, 'curl': 0.05, **o})
def MASK(pid, at, breath=None, who='mec'): return P(pid, 'noFaceSheet', on={'actor': who, 'joint': 'head', 'offset': [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, opts={'at': at, **({'breath': breath} if breath else {})})
def SKY(pid, pos, ry, **o): return P(pid, 'noPaperSky', pos=list(pos), ry=ry, opts=o)

# ============================== the hero
HF = {'lid': 0.35, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.1}
GAGS = [('S01', 0.5, 'mec', 'rubber neck'), ('S01b', 0.55, 'mec', 'flap'), ('S02', 0.95, 'mec', 'slap'), ('S02b', 0.6, 'mec', 'head pops out'), ('S04c', 0.5, 'p3', 'scratch'),
        ('S05b', 1.2, 'serveur', 'asleep'), ('S06b', 0.6, 'meteo', 'points up'), ('S07', 1.4, 'p2', 'belly'), ('S08b', 1.0, 'ministre', 'crab'), ('S10', 0.7, 'medecin', 'blister'),
        ('S12', 0.85, 'pharmacien', 'flick'), ('S12c', 1.0, 'arbitre', 'whistle'), ('S13', 0.75, 'ministre', 'cured'), ('S14', 0.6, 'mec', 'asks'), ('S15b', 0.3, 'mec', 'blank'),
        ('S16', 1.15, 'mec', 'slap again'), ('S16b', 1.0, 'pharmacien', 'pinch')]
for g_ in GAGS: st.gag(*g_)

# ============================== the kitchen (kitchenDay: back wall z -3.6, counter, fridge at x -2.7, a lamp hanging at (0, 2.7, -1.0))
KSET = {}
TILES = lambda n: P(f'carrelage{n}', 'ttTileOffset', pos=[0, 0, 0])
H1 = [0.0, 0.0, -0.55]; CHAIR1 = [0.0, 0.0, -0.6]; TAB = [0.0, 0.0, 0.15]; TTOP = 0.76
def KITCHEN(n, table=True):
    out = [TILES(n)]
    if table: out += [P(f'table{n}', 'table', pos=TAB, opts={'w': 1.7, 'd': 1.2, 'color': '#F2EEE6', 'legs': '#8E6A48'}), P(f'chaise{n}', 'chair', pos=CHAIR1, opts={'color': '#2F7F8C'})]
    return out
SIT = lambda: k(0.0, clip='sit')

# 1: « Ce mec voulait vérifier la dose. » At his kitchen table, waist up: he lifts the box to his chest square to us (an overshoot); his neck stretches
#    like rubber toward it to check (a squint, a tremble); on « dose » it snaps back with a squash; a blink
D1 = st.dur('S01'); DOSE1 = W('S01', 'L01', 5)
F1 = [0.35, 1.48, 2.35]; L1 = [0.0, 1.3, -0.4]
C1 = cam(0.0, F1, add(F1, [-0.04, 0.0, -0.14]), L1, L1, lens=40, ease='inOut')
BXA1 = [0.0, 0.96, -0.12]; BX1 = [0.0, 1.1, -0.1]; RYB1 = yaw(BX1, F1)
chkc('S01', C1, {'top': add(H1, [0, 1.92, 0]), 'chin': add(H1, [0, 1.33, 0]), 'box': BX1, 'boxL': add(BX1, [-0.18, -0.12, 0]), 'lamp': [0, 2.55, -1.0], 'table': [0.8, TTOP, 0.45]})
BM1 = [(0.04, BX1, 0.18, 'out')]; BT1 = track(BXA1, BM1)
SQZ1 = {'lid': 0.65, 'low': 0.35, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': -0.5}
HERO1 = [SIT(), k(-0.5, look=add(BX1, [0, 0.0, 0.25])), k(0.0, toon={**BOXK(BXA1, RYB1), 'face': HF}, toonDur=0.0),
         *[k(r(0.04 + 0.06 * j), toon={**BOXK(BT1(r(0.04 + 0.06 * j + 0.05)), RYB1), 'sq': [0.97, 1.04, 0.97], 'face': {**HF, 'brow': 0.5, 'lid': 0.2}}, toonDur=0.05) for j in range(3)],
         # the rubber neck: the head shoots forward and down toward the box on a neck twice its length, squinting, trembling
         k(0.24, toon={**BOXK(BX1, RYB1), 'sq': [1.04, 0.97, 1.04], 'bend': {'spine': [0.08, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {**HF, 'brow': 0.2}}, toonDur=0.05),
         k(0.3, toon={**BOXK(BX1, RYB1), 'bend': {'spine': [0.22, 0, 0, 1, None], 'neck': [0.62, 0, 0, 2.1, 0.85]}, 'face': SQZ1}, toonDur=0.14, toonEase='outBack'),
         *[k(r(0.48 + 0.067 * j), toon={**BOXK(BX1, RYB1), 'bend': {'spine': [0.22, 0, 0, 1, None], 'neck': [0.62 + 0.03 * (j % 2), 0, 0.05 * (1 - 2 * (j % 2)), 2.1 - 0.06 * (j % 2), 0.85]},
                                       'face': {**SQZ1, 'gx': 0.3 * (1 - 2 * (j % 3 == 0))}}, toonDur=0.05) for j in range(int((DOSE1 - 0.54) / 0.067))],
         # « dose »: the neck snaps home, a squash, the eyes spring open
         k(r(DOSE1 - 0.02), toon={**BOXK(BX1, RYB1), 'sq': [1.1, 0.9, 1.1], 'bend': {'neck': [-0.12, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {'lid': 0.0, 'eye': 0.35, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.8}}, toonDur=0.04, toonEase='out'),
         k(r(DOSE1 + 0.02), look='camera', lookDur=0.1),
         k(r(DOSE1 + 0.12), toon={**BOXK(BX1, RYB1), 'sq': [0.97, 1.03, 0.97], 'face': {**HF, 'brow': 0.5}}, toonDur=0.08),
         *life(r(DOSE1 + 0.24), D1, {**HF, 'brow': 0.4}, BOXK(BX1, RYB1), blinks=[r(DOSE1 + 0.3)], period=0.5)]
st.shot('S01', 'kitchenDay', setOpts=KSET, actors=[act('mec', H1, 0, 'sit', 'neutral', keys=HERO1)],
        props=[*KITCHEN(1), BOX('boite1', BXA1, F1, keys=MOVES(BM1))], cams=[C1])
st.cue('sfx:paper', 'S01', 0.05, 0.15); st.cue('sfx:stretch', 'S01', 0.3, 0.2); st.cue('sfx:pop', 'S01', r(DOSE1 - 0.02), 0.25)

# 1b: « Il a déplié la notice. » A lower three-quarter: the lid flips open, he pulls the tiny folded leaflet out with his right hand, one shake, FLAP: it
#     bursts open flat over the table with an overshoot and a ripple and drops onto it; he is blown back (a stretch, hair up); the box stays up in his left
#     hand, square to us
D1b = st.dur('S01b'); DEP1b = W('S01b', 'L01', 8)
F1b, L1b, LN1b = FIT([-0.5, 1.5, 2.2], {'top': [0, 1.92, -0.55], 'box': [-0.3, 1.18, -0.13], 'sf': [0.65, 0.76, 0.5], 'sn': [-0.65, 0.76, 0.5], 'sb': [0.65, 0.76, -0.4]}, back=True, margin=0.05, top=0.1, bottom=0.76, level=False, inside=(-6.5, 6.5, 0.3, 4.5, -3.3, 8))
C1b = cam(0.0, F1b, add(F1b, [0.05, 0.0, -0.1]), L1b, L1b, lens=LN1b, ease='inOut')
BX1b = off(H1, 0, 0.42, -0.3, 1.18); RYB1b = yaw(BX1b, F1b)
LF0 = add(BX1b, [0.0, 0.16, 0.0]); LF1 = off(H1, 0, 0.5, 0.12, 1.42); FLAP1b = 0.44; LFOPEN = [0.0, 0.98, 0.05]; LFTAB = [0.0, TTOP + 0.012, 0.05]
chkc('S01b', C1b, {'top': add(H1, [0, 1.92, 0]), 'chin': add(H1, [0, 1.33, 0]), 'box': BX1b, 'leafHand': LF1, 'sheetFar': [0.65, TTOP, 0.5], 'sheetNear': [-0.65, TTOP, 0.5], 'sheetBack': [0.65, TTOP, -0.4]})
LM1b = [(0.06, LF1, 0.16, 'out'), *[(r(0.24 + 0.05 * j), add(LF1, [0.05 * (1 - 2 * (j % 2)), 0.02 * (j % 2), 0.0]), 0.04, 'inOut') for j in range(3)],
        (FLAP1b, LFOPEN, 0.07, 'out'), (r(FLAP1b + 0.12), LFTAB, 0.16, 'in')]
LT1b = track(LF0, LM1b)
FL1b = {'lid': 0.0, 'eye': 0.5, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 1.0}
HERO1b = [SIT(), k(-0.5, look=add(LF1, [0, 0.1, 0.1])), k(0.0, toon={**BOXL(BX1b, RYB1b, add(LF0, [0, 0.03, -0.02]), 'pinch'), 'face': {**HF, 'brow': 0.3}}, toonDur=0.0),
          *[k(r(0.06 + 0.05 * j), toon={**BOXL(BX1b, RYB1b, add(LT1b(r(0.06 + 0.05 * j + 0.04)), [0, 0.0, -0.02]), 'pinch'), 'face': {**HF, 'brow': 0.4}}, toonDur=0.04) for j in range(int((FLAP1b - 0.06) / 0.05))],
          # FLAP: the sheet bursts open; he is blown back, stretched, hair up, the right hand flung up and out
          k(r(FLAP1b - 0.04), toon={**BOXL(BX1b, RYB1b, LF1, 'pinch'), 'sq': [1.05, 0.95, 1.05], 'face': {**HF, 'lid': 0.6}}, toonDur=0.03),
          k(FLAP1b, toon={**BOXL(BX1b, RYB1b, off(H1, 0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.75), 'spread'), 'sq': [0.88, 1.16, 0.88], 'hairUp': 1.0, 'bend': {'spine': [-0.22, 0, 0, 1, None], 'neck': [-0.25, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': FL1b}, toonDur=0.04, toonEase='out'),
          k(r(FLAP1b + 0.04), look=[0.0, 1.1, 0.6], lookDur=0.08),
          k(r(FLAP1b + 0.22), toon={**BOXL(BX1b, RYB1b, off(H1, 0, 0.35, 0.35, 1.25), 'open'), 'sq': [1.03, 0.97, 1.03], 'hairUp': 0.5, 'bend': {'spine': [-0.08, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {**FL1b, 'eye': 0.3, 'brow': 0.8}}, toonDur=0.1),
          k(r(FLAP1b + 0.4), look='camera', lookDur=0.15),
          *life(r(FLAP1b + 0.45), D1b, {**HF, 'brow': 0.7, 'lid': 0.1}, BOXL(BX1b, RYB1b, off(H1, 0, 0.35, 0.3, 1.0), 'open'), blinks=[r(D1b - 0.3)], period=0.5)]
st.shot('S01b', 'kitchenDay', setOpts=KSET, actors=[act('mec', H1, 0, 'sit', 'neutral', keys=HERO1b)],
        props=[*KITCHEN('1b'), BOX('boite1b', BX1b, F1b, open=[[0, 0.0], [0.05, 1.0]]),
               LEAF('notice1b', LF0, w=1.3, h=0.9, unfold=[[0, 0], [FLAP1b, 0], [r(FLAP1b + 0.07), 1.25, 'lin'], [r(FLAP1b + 0.17), 0.94], [r(FLAP1b + 0.27), 1.0]],
                    flap=[[FLAP1b, 1.4], [r(FLAP1b + 0.5), 0.15]], keys=MOVES(LM1b))],
        cams=[C1b])
st.cue('sfx:click', 'S01b', 0.05, 0.15); st.cue('sfx:paper', 'S01b', 0.25, 0.15); st.cue('sfx:paper', 'S01b', FLAP1b, 0.5); st.cue('whoosh', 'S01b', FLAP1b, 0.2, 0.3, 300, 2500); st.cue('sfx:pop', 'S01b', FLAP1b, 0.2)

# 2: « Impossible de la replier. » High over the table: he folds the sheet in half (both hands carry its near edge over in an arc, his arms stretched),
#    it puffs up like a pillow, he slams it flat with both mittens (a squash), it springs open twice as big and flies into his face: the leaflet flat
#    over his face like a mask; his head knocked back, his arms flailing
D2 = st.dur('S02')
BX2 = [-0.38, TTOP + 0.125, 0.64]
F2, L2, LN2 = FIT([0.15, 2.45, 2.2], {'top': [0, 2.02, -0.45], 'snR': [0.62, TTOP, 0.52], 'snL': [-0.62, TTOP, 0.52], 'box': add(BX2, [0, 0.13, 0]), 'boxb': add(BX2, [0, -0.12, 0]), 'arc': [0, 1.25, 0.05]}, margin=0.05, top=0.07, bottom=0.76)
C2 = cam(0.0, F2, add(F2, [-0.03, -0.03, -0.08]), L2, L2, lens=LN2, ease='inOut')
CZ = 0.05; HL2 = 0.45
def edge2(f): th = f * PI; return [0.0, r(TTOP + 0.012 + HL2 * math.sin(th)), r(CZ - HL2 * math.cos(th))]
F0_, F1_ = 0.04, 0.34; PUFF2, PRESS2, SPRING2, SLAP2 = 0.36, 0.6, 0.8, 0.88
chkc('S02', C2, {'top': add(H1, [0, 1.92, 0]), 'face': add(H1, [0, 1.6, 0.1]), 'box': BX2, 'sheetNear': [0.65, TTOP, 0.5], 'sheetFarL': [-0.65, TTOP, -0.4], 'foldTop': edge2(0.5)})
def E2(f, dx): e = edge2(f); return [r(e[0] + dx), r(e[1] + 0.02), r(e[2] - 0.02)]
PRS2 = lambda dx: [dx, TTOP + 0.06, 0.28]
UP2L, UP2R = off(H1, 0, 0.55, -0.55, 1.75), off(H1, 0, 0.55, 0.55, 1.75)
HERO2 = [SIT(), k(-0.5, look=[0.0, TTOP, 0.0]), k(0.0, toon={**HAND(E2(0, -0.35), E2(0, 0.35), 'grip', 'grip'), 'bend': {'spine': [0.2, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {**HF, 'brow': -0.3}}, toonDur=0.0),
         # the fold: both hands carry the near edge over in an arc, the spine bending after it, the arms stretching
         *[k(r(F0_ + (F1_ - F0_) * j / 6), toon={**HAND(E2(j / 6, -0.35), E2(j / 6, 0.35), 'grip', 'grip'), 'hose': 0.15, 'bend': {'spine': [r(0.2 + 0.3 * j / 6), 0, 0, 1, None], 'neck': [0.2, 0, 0, 1, None]},
                                                    'face': {**HF, 'brow': -0.5, 'lid': 0.5}}, toonDur=0.05) for j in range(7)],
         # the pillow: the folded sheet puffs up, his hands spring off it, eyes wide
         k(PUFF2, toon={**HAND(add(E2(1, -0.4), [0, 0.25, -0.1]), add(E2(1, 0.4), [0, 0.25, -0.1]), 'open', 'open'), 'sq': [0.95, 1.06, 0.95], 'bend': {'spine': [0.1, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {'lid': 0.0, 'eye': 0.35, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.8}}, toonDur=0.06, toonEase='out'),
         # the slam: both mittens straight down on it, the whole body squashes
         k(r(PRESS2 - 0.08), toon={**HAND(add(PRS2(-0.2), [0, 0.35, 0]), add(PRS2(0.2), [0, 0.35, 0]), 'open', 'open'), 'sq': [0.95, 1.07, 0.95], 'bend': {'spine': [0.25, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {**HF, 'brow': -0.8, 'lid': 0.5, 'mouth': 'clench'}}, toonDur=0.06),
         k(PRESS2, toon={**HAND(PRS2(-0.2), PRS2(0.2), 'open', 'open'), 'sq': [1.12, 0.88, 1.12], 'bend': {'spine': [0.42, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {**HF, 'brow': -0.9, 'lid': 0.7, 'mouth': 'clench'}}, toonDur=0.03, toonEase='out'),
         k(r(PRESS2 + 0.1), toon={**HAND(PRS2(-0.2), PRS2(0.2), 'open', 'open'), 'sq': [1.02, 0.98, 1.02], 'bend': {'spine': [0.35, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {**HF, 'mouth': 'smirk', 'brow': 0.3}}, toonDur=0.08),
         # it springs open and slaps him in the face: his head knocked back, his arms thrown up, flailing
         k(SLAP2, toon={**HAND(UP2L, UP2R, 'spread', 'spread'), 'sq': [1.14, 0.86, 1.14], 'hairUp': 0.9, 'bend': {'spine': [-0.28, 0, 0, 1, None], 'neck': [-0.4, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': HF}, toonDur=0.03, toonEase='out'),
         *[k(r(SLAP2 + 0.08 + 0.07 * j), toon={**HAND(add(UP2L, [0.08 * (1 - 2 * (j % 2)), -0.1 * (j % 2), 0.05]), add(UP2R, [-0.08 * (1 - 2 * (j % 2)), -0.1 * ((j + 1) % 2), 0.05]), 'spread', 'spread'),
                                                'sq': [0.97, 1.03, 0.97] if j % 2 else [1.02, 0.98, 1.02], 'bend': {'spine': [-0.18, 0, 0, 1, None], 'neck': [-0.22, 0.12 * (1 - 2 * (j % 2)), 0, 1, None]}, 'face': HF}, toonDur=0.05) for j in range(int((D2 - SLAP2 - 0.1) / 0.07))]]
LK2 = [k(0.0, visible=True), k(r(SPRING2 - 0.01), to=[0.0, TTOP + 0.3, -0.12], dur=0.07, ease='out'), k(r(SPRING2 - 0.01), rotTo=[-0.5, 0.0, 0.0], dur=0.07), k(r(SLAP2 - 0.005), visible=False)]
st.shot('S02', 'kitchenDay', setOpts=KSET, actors=[act('mec', H1, 0, 'sit', 'neutral', keys=HERO2)],
        props=[*KITCHEN(2), BOX('boite2', BX2, F2),
               LEAF('notice2', LFTAB, w=1.3, h=0.9, fold=[[0, 0], [F0_, 0], [F1_, 1.0, 'lin'], [r(SPRING2 - 0.02), 1.0], [r(SPRING2 + 0.04), 0.0]],
                    bulge=[[0, 0], [F1_, 0], [r(PUFF2 + 0.06), 1.15], [r(PUFF2 + 0.14), 0.95], [r(PRESS2 - 0.02), 1.0], [r(PRESS2 + 0.02), 0.0, 'lin']],
                    unfold=[[0, 1], [r(SPRING2), 1], [r(SLAP2), 2.0, 'lin']], flap=[[SPRING2, 0], [r(SPRING2 + 0.04), 1.5]], keys=LK2),
               MASK('masque2', SLAP2, breath=[[0, 0], [1.1, 0.0], [1.22, 1.0], [D2, -0.4]])],
        cams=[C2])
st.cue('sfx:paper', 'S02', 0.05, 0.3); st.cue('sfx:stretch', 'S02', PUFF2, 0.2); st.cue('thud', 'S02', PRESS2, 0.35); st.cue('whoosh', 'S02', SPRING2, 0.2, 0.2, 300, 2500); st.cue('sfx:splat', 'S02', SLAP2, 0.45); st.cue('sfx:paper', 'S02', r(SLAP2 + 0.02), 0.3)

# 2b: « Elle a recouvert la cuisine. » The kitchen papered from floor to ceiling, the paper draped over the fridge, the counter and the cupboards,
#     curling at the top: his head pops out of a heap of paper like a cork (the petals spring out), then the box pops out beside it, square to us; a blink,
#     his eyes slide to the wall and back
D2b = st.dur('S02b')
H2b = [0.45, 0.0, -1.2]
F2b = [1.55, 1.85, 3.55]; L2b = [0.0, 1.62, -1.9]
C2b = cam(0.0, F2b, add(F2b, [-0.05, 0.0, -0.18]), L2b, L2b, lens=50, ease='inOut')
RY2b = r(yaw(H2b, F2b) * 0.8)
POP2b, BOXUP2b = 0.06, 0.34
BXD2b = off(H2b, RY2b, 0.1, -0.44, 1.2); BX2b = off(H2b, RY2b, 0.12, -0.44, 2.02); RYB2b = yaw(BX2b, F2b)
chkc('S02b', C2b, {'top': add(H2b, [0, 2.3, 0]), 'chin': add(H2b, [0, 1.77, 0]), 'box': BX2b, 'curlL': [-2.5, 3.3, -3.4], 'curlR': [2.5, 3.3, -3.4], 'fridge': [-2.7, 2.0, -3.0], 'counter': [0.9, 0.95, -3.0], 'floor': [1.0, 0.0, 0.6]})
BUB = {'lid': 0.4, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.2}
BOXH2b = lambda p: HAND(add(p, [0.0, -0.13, -0.03]), None, 'grip', 'rest')
HERO2b = [k(-0.5, look='camera'), k(0.0, to=add(H2b, [0, -0.6, 0]), dur=0.0, glide=True, face=RY2b), k(POP2b, to=H2b, dur=0.08, glide=True, ease='out', face=RY2b, auto=0),
          k(0.0, toon={**BOXH2b(BXD2b), 'auto': 0, 'sq': [0.9, 1.1, 0.9], 'face': {**BUB, 'lid': 0.9}}, toonDur=0.0),
          # the cork pop: stretched on the way up, a squash as he stops, an overshoot
          k(POP2b, toon={**BOXH2b(BXD2b), 'auto': 0, 'sq': [0.86, 1.18, 0.86], 'hairUp': 1.0, 'face': {'lid': 0.0, 'eye': 0.3, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.9}}, toonDur=0.04, toonEase='out'),
          k(r(POP2b + 0.1), toon={**BOXH2b(BXD2b), 'auto': 0, 'sq': [1.1, 0.9, 1.1], 'hairUp': 0.6, 'face': {'lid': 0.2, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.5}}, toonDur=0.04),
          k(r(POP2b + 0.18), toon={**BOXH2b(BXD2b), 'sq': [0.97, 1.03, 0.97], 'face': BUB}, toonDur=0.06),
          # the box pops out beside his head
          k(BOXUP2b, toon={**BOXH2b(BX2b), 'face': BUB}, toonDur=0.08, toonEase='outBack'),
          k(0.62, toon={**BOXH2b(BX2b), 'face': {**BUB, 'gx': 0.85}}, toonDur=0.12), k(0.92, toon={**BOXH2b(BX2b), 'face': {**BUB, 'gx': -0.6, 'gy': -0.3}}, toonDur=0.12),
          k(1.12, toon={**BOXH2b(BX2b), 'face': BUB}, toonDur=0.1), *blink(1.2, BUB, BOXH2b(BX2b))]
st.shot('S02b', 'kitchenDay', setOpts=KSET, actors=[act('mec', add(H2b, [0, -0.6, 0]), RY2b, 'stand', 'neutral', keys=HERO2b)],
        props=[TILES('2b'), P('papier2b', 'noPaperRoom', pos=[0, 0, 0], opts={'mound': [H2b[0], H2b[2]], 'burst': [r(POP2b + 0.02)], 'mh': 1.72}),
               BOX('boite2b', BXD2b, F2b, keys=[k(BOXUP2b, to=BX2b, dur=0.12, ease='out'), k(r(BOXUP2b + 0.1), squash=[0.9, 1.15, 1.0], dur=0.35)])],
        cams=[C2b])
st.cue('sfx:pop', 'S02b', POP2b, 0.35); st.cue('sfx:paper', 'S02b', 0.02, 0.25); st.cue('sfx:pop', 'S02b', BOXUP2b, 0.22); st.cue('sfx:boing', 'S02b', r(POP2b + 0.1), 0.1)

# 3: « Puis l'immeuble. » A building front from the far pavement, looking up: tongues of lined paper burst out of its windows one after the other from the
#    top floor, the whole building swells twice
D3 = st.dur('S03')
FAC = [8.4, 0.0, 0.0]
F3 = [-7.2, 1.7, -4.6]; L3 = [8.4, 9.2, 0.6]
C3 = cam(0.0, F3, add(F3, [0.3, 0.1, 0.1]), L3, L3, lens=54, ease='inOut')
chkc('S03', C3, {'roofL': [8.4, 17.3, -5.0], 'roofR': [8.4, 17.3, 5.0], 'chim': [8.4, 19.4, 3.3], 'footL': [8.4, 0.0, -5.0], 'footR': [8.4, 0.0, 5.0], 'win1': [8.3, 4.0, 3.75]})
SSET = {'eiffel': False, 'clouds': 6}
st.shot('S03', 'parisStreet', setOpts={**SSET, 'clear': [-12, 12], 'clearL': [-14, 6]},
        props=[P('facade3', 'noFacade', pos=FAC, ry=-90, opts={'w': 10, 'floors': 5, 'cols': 4, 'pop': 0.04, 'stagger': 0.042, 'color': '#F2DCCB'},
                 keys=[k(0.2, squash=[1.0, 1.035, 1.05], dur=0.5), k(0.62, squash=[1.0, 1.05, 1.07], dur=0.5)])], cams=[C3])
for i in range(4): st.cue('sfx:pop', 'S03', r(0.04 + 0.042 * 4 * i), 0.18)
st.cue('sfx:paper', 'S03', 0.1, 0.35); st.cue('sfx:boing', 'S03', 0.62, 0.12)

# 3b: « Puis la rue. » The street at pavement height: the leaflet rolls down the pavement toward us like a carpet, a pigeon running on top of the roll,
#     flapping to keep its balance
D3b = st.dur('S03b')
CX3 = 7.2; Z03 = -47.0; LEN03 = 36.0; SP3 = 7.0; RR3 = 0.3
F3b = [6.85, 0.95, 1.6]; L3b = [7.2, 0.72, -6.0]
C3b = cam(0.0, F3b, add(F3b, [0.0, 0.0, 0.15]), L3b, L3b, lens=44, ease='inOut')
z3 = lambda t: r(Z03 + LEN03 + SP3 * t)
chkc('S03b', C3b, {'roll0': [CX3, 0.3, z3(0)], 'roll1': [CX3, 0.3, z3(D3b)], 'rollEdge1': [CX3 + 1.1, 0.3, z3(D3b)], 'pigeon1': [CX3, 0.9, z3(D3b)], 'far': [CX3, 0.0, -30.0]})
st.shot('S03b', 'parisStreet', setOpts={**SSET, 'clear': [-40, 10], 'clearL': [-40, 10]},
        props=[P('tapis3b', 'noPaperCarpet', pos=[CX3, 0.0, Z03], opts={'w': 2.2, 'r': RR3, 'len0': LEN03, 'speed': SP3}),
               P('pigeon3b', 'pigeon', pos=[CX3, 2 * RR3 + 0.012, z3(0)], ry=15, scale=1.6, opts={'big': True, 'flaps': [[0.05, 0.4], [0.55, D3b]], 'headYaw': -0.3},
                 keys=[k(0.0, to=[CX3, 2 * RR3 + 0.012, z3(D3b)], dur=D3b, ease='linear'), *[k(r(0.12 + 0.24 * j), squash=[1.15, 0.85, 1.0], dur=0.25) for j in range(3)]])],
        cams=[C3b])
st.cue('engine', 'S03b', 0.0, 0.06, D3b); st.cue('sfx:paper', 'S03b', 0.1, 0.25); st.cue('sfx:squeak', 'S03b', 0.3, 0.12)

# ============================== the passers-by on the pavement (right-hand pavement of parisStreet, x ~ 6-9)
PAPER4 = [6.9, 0.0, -2.0]
P4 = {'p1': [5.85, 0.0, -2.95], 'p2': [6.6, 0.0, -3.3], 'p3': [7.4, 0.0, -3.25], 'p4': [8.15, 0.0, -2.85]}
F4 = [5.1, 1.4, 3.3]; L4 = [7.94, 0.258, -6.22]
C4 = cam(0.0, F4, add(F4, [0.05, 0.0, -0.15]), L4, L4, lens=44, ease='inOut')
RY4 = {n: r(yaw(p, F4) * 0.85) for n, p in P4.items()}
BENT = lambda tw=0.0, s=0.5, n=0.42: {'spine': [s, 0, 0, 1, None], 'neck': [n, 0, tw, 1, None]}
PF = {'p1': {'lid': 0.45, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.1}, 'p2': {'lid': 0.5, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': -0.2}, 'p3': {'lid': 0.4, 'mouth': 'o', 'brow': 0.3}, 'p4': {'lid': 0.55, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.0}}
PHANDS = lambda n, p: HAND(off(p, RY4[n], 0.12, 0.2, 0.95), off(p, RY4[n], 0.12, -0.2, 0.95), 'rest', 'rest')

# 4: « Les passants ont lu : » Four passers-by bent over the paper on the pavement read it like typewriters: their heads sweep along a line together
#    and snap back with a bell, twice
D4 = st.dur('S04')
chkc('S04', C4, {**{f'{n}top': add(p, [0, 2.15, 0]) for n, p in P4.items()}, 'paperNear': [6.9, 0, -0.5], 'paperL': [4.9, 0, -2.0]})
SWEEP = [(0.0, 0.42), (0.47, 0.42)]
act4 = []
for n, p in P4.items():
    ks = [k(-0.5, look=add(PAPER4, [0, 0.4, 0])), k(0.0, toon={**PHANDS(n, p), 'bend': BENT(0.28), 'face': {**PF[n], 'gx': 0.5}}, toonDur=0.0)]
    for t0, d in SWEEP:
        ks += [k(r(t0 + 0.02), toon={**PHANDS(n, p), 'bend': BENT(0.28), 'face': {**PF[n], 'gx': 0.55}}, toonDur=0.04),
               k(r(t0 + 0.06), toon={**PHANDS(n, p), 'bend': BENT(-0.28), 'face': {**PF[n], 'gx': -0.55}}, toonDur=r(d - 0.06), toonEase='linear'),
               k(r(t0 + d + 0.01), toon={**PHANDS(n, p), 'sq': [1.03, 0.97, 1.03], 'bend': BENT(0.3, n=0.5), 'face': {**PF[n], 'gx': 0.6, 'lid': 0.2}}, toonDur=0.04, toonEase='out')]
    ks += blink(r(0.95 + 0.03 * len(act4)), PF[n], {**PHANDS(n, p), 'bend': BENT(0.3)})
